# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example                                    | Total number of qubits | Ansatz   | RMSE                       | Classical compute time (min) | QPU time (min) |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Inviscid Burgers' equation                 | 4                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0147                     | ~1                           | 11             |\n"
"| Pressureless Euler's equations             | 8                      | `HEA`    | 0.0193                     | ~1.5                         | 10             |\n"
"| Hypoelastic 1D tensile test                | 6                      | `HEA`    | 0.0296                     | ~1                           | 10             |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, 1 asset            | 6                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0084                     | ~0.3                         | 5.0            |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, basket of 2 assets | 7                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0085                     | ~4                           | 12.0           |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, basket of 3 assets | 9                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0104                     | ~67                          | 20.7           |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Contoh                                     | Jumlah bilangan qubit  | Ansatz   | RMSE                       | Masa pengiraan klasik (min)  | Masa QPU (min) |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Persamaan Burgers' tak likat               | 4                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0147                     | ~1                           | 11             |\n"
"| Persamaan Euler tanpa tekanan              | 8                      | `HEA`    | 0.0193                     | ~1.5                         | 10             |\n"
"| Ujian tegangan 1D hipoelastik              | 6                      | `HEA`    | 0.0296                     | ~1                           | 10             |\n"
"| Persamaan Black-Scholes, 1 aset            | 6                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0084                     | ~0.3                         | 5.0            |\n"
"| Persamaan Black-Scholes, bakul 2 aset      | 7                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0085                     | ~4                           | 12.0           |\n"
"| Persamaan Black-Scholes, bakul 3 aset      | 9                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0104                     | ~67                          | 20.7           |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The RMSE is the Root Mean Square Error between the solution and the reference solution (aggregated over the two functions for the Euler, and tensile test cases). For the Burgers, Euler, and tensile test cases, it is measured on the QPU over the sampled points. For the Black-Scholes cases, it is computed inside the domain, excluding the final time and the edges where the solution is imposed, on a fine grid (600 points per axis for 1 asset, 80 for 2 assets, 16 for 3 assets), by noiseless simulation at the parameters retained on the QPU. The classical compute time is the time spent by the optimizers on the classical side of the hybrid loop. It is mostly due to the evaluation of the points on the grid, which is easily parallelizable. The QPU time is the quantum processing time billed for the optimization jobs.\n"
msgstr "RMSE ialah Root Mean Square Error antara penyelesaian dan penyelesaian rujukan (diagregatkan merentasi dua fungsi bagi kes Euler dan ujian tegangan). Bagi kes Burgers, Euler dan ujian tegangan, ia diukur pada QPU pada titik yang disampel. Bagi kes Black-Scholes, ia dikira di dalam domain, tidak termasuk masa akhir dan tepi tempat penyelesaian dikenakan, pada grid halus (600 titik bagi setiap paksi untuk 1 aset, 80 untuk 2 aset, 16 untuk 3 aset), melalui simulasi tanpa hingar pada parameter yang dikekalkan pada QPU. Masa pengiraan klasik ialah masa yang diambil oleh pengoptimum pada bahagian klasik gelung hibrid. Ia kebanyakannya disebabkan oleh penilaian titik pada grid, yang mudah diselarikan. Masa QPU ialah masa pemprosesan kuantum yang dibilkan untuk job pengoptimuman.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of qubits is lower than in the previous version. The circuit binding feature reduces the QPU time of the runs, not the number of qubits. It remains possible to increase the number of qubits by executing several circuits in parallel, which reduces the QPU time needed even further, and the new version of the function leaves room to scale to larger numbers of qubits and larger problems.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan qubit lebih rendah berbanding versi sebelumnya. Ciri pengikatan litar mengurangkan masa QPU bagi larian, bukan bilangan qubit. Masih boleh meningkatkan bilangan qubit dengan melaksanakan beberapa litar secara selari, yang mengurangkan lagi masa QPU yang diperlukan, dan versi baharu fungsi ini memberi ruang untuk berskala kepada bilangan qubit yang lebih besar dan masalah yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The optimization steps of these runs are described as follows:\n"
"- The `popsize` argument is the number of candidates evaluated at each generation of `CMAES`.\n"
"- The `CMAES` stages can stop early when the cost stagnates.\n"
"- A cost evaluation is the computation of the cost function for one set of circuit parameters, measured on the QPU with the number of shots of the stage.\n"
"- A `CMAES` generation is made of `popsize` evaluations, so the iterations of `CMAES` are counted in generations.\n"
"- An `LS-TRF` iteration computes the Jacobian of the cost function at the current point, with the parameter-shift rule (PSR) here, and evaluates the cost function at one or several trial points.\n"
"- The Jacobian requires its own circuits (the parameter-shifted circuits), which are not counted as evaluations. The number of Jacobians is therefore the number of `LS-TRF` iterations, and the number of evaluations is higher than the number of iterations because some trial points are rejected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah pengoptimuman bagi larian ini diperihalkan seperti berikut:\n"
"- Argumen `popsize` ialah bilangan calon yang dinilai pada setiap generasi `CMAES`.\n"
"- Peringkat `CMAES` boleh berhenti awal apabila kos tidak lagi berubah.\n"
"- Penilaian kos ialah pengiraan fungsi kos bagi satu set parameter litar, diukur pada QPU dengan bilangan shot peringkat tersebut.\n"
"- Satu generasi `CMAES` terdiri daripada `popsize` penilaian, jadi lelaran `CMAES` dikira dalam generasi.\n"
"- Satu lelaran `LS-TRF` mengira Jacobian bagi fungsi kos pada titik semasa, dengan petua parameter-shift (PSR) di sini, dan menilai fungsi kos pada satu atau beberapa titik cubaan.\n"
"- Jacobian memerlukan litarnya sendiri (litar yang dianjak parameter), yang tidak dikira sebagai penilaian. Oleh itu, bilangan Jacobian ialah bilangan lelaran `LS-TRF`, dan bilangan penilaian lebih tinggi daripada bilangan lelaran kerana sesetengah titik cubaan ditolak.\n"

